N2  - Antiplatelet agents comprise a critical component in the multi-modality treatment of ischemic heart disease. In addition to anticholesterol, beta-blocking, and angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibiting agents as well as mechanical intervention, platelet inhibition has resulted in improved outcomes for patients with ischemic heart disease. Platelet aggregation and resultant thrombus formation is a multi-step process with several points of potential intervention. As this pathway has been elucidated, more opportunities to intervene pharmacologically have become apparent. © 2012 Springer-Verlag Berlin Heidelberg.
