N2  - The time is ripe to assess whether pharmacogenomics research - the study of the genetic basis for variation in drug response - has provided important insights into a personalized approach to prescribing and dosing medications. Here, we describe the status of the f eld and approaches for addressing some of the open questions in pharmacogenomics research and use of genetic testing in guiding drug therapy.
