N2  - One of the mainstays of the treatment of acute coronary syndromes is the interference of thrombus formation. Over the past few years, much research has been dedicated to understanding the cellular mechanisms involved in the development of thrombus. This research has resulted in the identification of new pharmacologic targets for drug advancement as well as the development of more sophisticated versions of previously existing medications. In this article, we review the literature on the newest advances in oral antiplatelet therapies. © Touchbriefings 2011.
