N2  - The low reponse (LR) to clopidogrel (CL) is considered to increase risk for stent thrombosis (ST). Because cytochrome P450 system (CYP) is essential to the generation of active metabolite of CL, polymorphic variations of CYP may influence the response to CL. In this non-randomized and single-center study (134 pts,age 56+9.9 yrs),we assessed whether single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) of CYP2C19, CYP3A5 and CYP2C9 related to CLLR and risk of events including definite ST (dST), stroke (S) and bleeding after primary,urgent or elective BMS or DES placement. Platelet aggregation (PA) was assessed by multiplate analyser (MPA). All pts received a prePCI CL loading dose of 600 mg.The duration of CL treatment was 9 to12 months (m) for BMS, and >12 m for DES.The daily dose of CLwas 150 mg for first week, and 75mg thereafter.Mean FU period was 660±230 days, and visits were performed within first 7 and 30 days, and 3, 6, 9 and 12 m after PCI. Definite STwas noted in 2 (%1.6) pts and within the first 22 days. TIMI major and minor bleeding were noted in 1.6% and 3.2% pts, respectively. None had S. Baseline PA (AU.min) to ADP (ADP-PA)was 293±247,and showed no difference compared with baseline values along the FU (p=NS).The PA was subdivided into quintiles, and the border of 5th quintile, 495 was defined as cut-off value for CLLR.The LR was noted in 20.3% of pts, and was associated with high platelet count (p=0.02) but not with other clinical,laboratory and procedural characteristics (p=NS).The SNP of CYP3A5 (A6986G) was noted in 7.5% of pts,and ADP-PA (p=NS) or LR% (30 vs 18.8,p=NS)were similar between pts with SNP and without.The CYP2C9 alleles were as follows; Normal and slow metabolizers (NM,SM) with 1∗1 or 1∗2 (78%) and 1∗3,2∗2 or 2∗3 (22%)alleles,respectively.Measures of ADP-PA (p=NS) and LR %(18.5 vs 31.3, p=NS) were similar among pts with NM and SMs.The SNP of CYP2C19 (G681A) genotypes were as follows; wild type 78%, heterozygous 22% and homozygous 0.7%. CYP2C19∗2. Homozygous or heterozygous genotypes compared with its wild type related to a higher ADP-PA (AU.min) (432±283 vs 250±220, p<0.01) and an increased LR% (OR:5.0;1.9-12.6,95% CI, p=0.001). Two out of the 11 pts (18%) with STwere heterozygous.Moreover, CYP2C19∗2 was an independent predictor for LR (OR:2.1, 95 CI:1.1-5.1, p=0.02). None of the CYP2C19, CYP2C9 or CYP3A5 variants was associated with stroke or bleeding risk (p=NS). Conclusions: In pts with long-term CL treatment after BMS or DES placement, CYP2C19 ∗2 allele but not CYP2C9 or CYP3A5 variants seemed to be associated with CLLR on MPA and risk for early ST. However, none of these SNPs related to long-term clinical outcome.
