N2  - Objectives: Prospective trial to assess which platelet function test is best to predict trombo-ischemic events in patients on clopidogrel treatment undergoing elective PCI with stent implantation. Background: Dual antiplatelet therapy reduces thrombotic complications in patients undergoing PCI. Nonetheless, ischemic events still occur and several studies have demonstrated a strong relationship between magnitude of high ontreatment platelet reactivity (HPR) and the occurrence adverse clinical outcome. However, previous studies are hampered by the fact that platelet function was evaluated by only one platelet function test. Methods: POPular included 1069 consecutive patients undergoing elective coronary stent implantation. All patients were pre-treated with clopidogrel. Ontreatment platelet reactivity was measured in parallel by Light Transmittance Aggregometry (using Adenosine Diphosphate (ADP) as agonists), the Coneand- platelet analyzer (ADP pre-stimulation), the PFA-100 (with the collagen/ ADP and the novel ADP-receptor specific INNOVANCE P2Y cartridges), the VerifyNow P2Y12 assay and the Plateletworks single cell counting method using ADP as agonist. The predictive value of the different platelet function tests to predict clinical outcome was established. Primary endpoint was all-cause death, non fatal myocardial infarction, ischemic stroke and stent thrombosis. Results: The results of the POPular-study will be presented as a Late Breaking Clinical Trial at the AHA in Orlando in November 2009. As a consequence, the results are under embargo and we can not provide any results at the time of the writing of this abstract. This is the largest prospective comparison of platelet function tests on clinical outcome and we hope the abstract selection committee will give us the opportunity to present the results of the POPular-study at the joint GTH & NVTH meeting.
