N2  - Background: Clopidogrel is a prodrug that has to be converted to an active metabolite by hepatic cytochrome P450 (CYP) isoenzyme to inhibit platelet aggregation. CYP2C19 polymorphism is reported to relate with clopidogrel resistance in coronary artery occlusive disease and some studies suggested that competitive inhibition of antiplatelet activity of clopidogrel by other drugs metabolized by same CYP isoenzymes. In this study, we sought to determine the relation of genetic polymorphism of CYP2C19 gene on clopidogrel resistance and effect of other drugs on clopidogrel resistance in cerebrovascular disease patient. Methods: Total 118 patients with cerebrovascular disease received daily 75mg clopidogrel for at least 5 days and underwent CYP genetic polymorphism analysis using Seelplex CYP2C19 ACE Genotyping system and clopidogrel resistance test using VerifyNow® P2Y12 system. Genetic polymorphisms were expressed as extensive (1∗ /1∗ allele), intermediate (1∗ /2∗ , 1∗ /3∗ alleles) and poor (2∗ /2∗ , 2∗ /3∗ , 3∗ /3∗ alleles) metabolizer groups, and clopidogrel response were expressed as P2Y12 reaction units (PRU) and high PRU value suggested clopidogrel resistance. Effect of other drugs such as calcium channel blocker (CCB) and statin on clopidogrel resistance was also evaluated. Results: The numbers of each metabolizer group were 54 (45.8%, extensive), 48 (40.7%, intermediate) and 16 (13.6%, poor). The PRU values showed increment from extensive to poor metabolizer groups (extensive 185.57± 81.25; intermediate 221.13± 91.22; poor 314.81± 58.18, p< 0.0001). Patients co-treated with CCB (n=43) and statin (n=79) showed higher PRU values compared to non users butwith no significance (CCB co-treated 233.49± 95.41, not-treated 208.43± 90.01; Statin co-treated 220.85± 100.46, not-treated 210.90± 74.19). Conclusion: Our study showed patient with CYP2C19∗ 2 and CYP2C19∗ 3 allele polymorphism (intermediate and poor metabolizer group) had clopidogrel resistance measured by PRU value. There was no statistical correlation between CCB and statin with clopidogrel resistance in this study.
