N2  - Clopidogrel is an antiplatelet agent that has established itself as a fundamental agent in the treatment of coronary artery disease for the prevention of thrombotic complications. The utility of clopidogrel has been evaluated in several clinical scenarios over the last decade. The benefits of dual antiplatelet therapy (clopidogrel plus aspirin) in patients undergoing percutaneous coronary interventions and in patients presenting with acute coronary syndromes are now well established. Long-term therapy up to 12 months may give additional cardiovascular protection in high-risk patients and following drug-eluting stent implantation. However, the optimal duration of clopidogrel therapy remains controversial. Recent studies suggest a new role for clopidogrel as adjunctive treatment in ST-elevation myocardial infarction following thrombolysis. © 2006 Informa UK Ltd.
