N2  - Platelets are key players in arterial thrombotic events such as ischemic stroke or myocardial infarction. ADP secreted from the platelet-dense granules plays a very vital role in amplifying the primary platelet activation, by interacting with its P2Y1 and P2Y12 receptors. Stimulation of the P2Y receptors leads to the activation of distinct intracellular signaling pathways that result in platelet activation. In this review we discuss the role of P2Y1 and P2Y12 receptors in the process of thrombus formation and provide an informative debate to understand which ADP receptor is a more suitable target for the development of antithrombotic agents. © 2005 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
